Original commit body from edde1333df9c8e8545a63b99586487713b95b260:

Read off the first heartbeat timeline of a cold self-run (8m38s, 6 cores).

Heartbeat format. Six workers on one comma-joined line were unreadable
(`, ` vs ` > ` separators, a leading … on each, `x2:1166` running the
recursion count into the line number, no pass name). Now one indented line
per busy worker, named by its pass via run_status.worker_pass, which the
analyzer pool (_run_named) and the linker chokepoint enter; innermost frame
only; sorted, capped at 8 (+N more). The main stack stays explicit and is
named by its pass when it runs one (serial linkers). Recursion reads
`:1166 (recursion x2)`.

Mislabelled phases. Fingerprint stamping ran after the linkers with no
marker, so "Running linkers 1m59s" included up to ~1m of it: now
"Stamping fingerprints". The sketch's source/test file collection ran under
"Loading cached profile": now "Sketch: Collecting source and test files".

Cold sketch re-walk (~1m on this repo). The survey ran inside
_generate_sketch_impl, after the wrapper had peeked the cache and found
nothing, so the cold sketch had no file index and every find_files walked
the disk. _discover_or_survey now runs it in the wrapper, which then
installs the same map-scoped index a warm run gets, and passes the loaded
map on (a warm run no longer parses survey.json twice). reports_run moves
to generate_sketch so the timeline stays one run. Cold and warm sketches
now agree: Structure lists the survey's file universe, so EMPTY directories
no longer appear on a cold run (warm runs already omitted them);
test_many_directories now gives its 15 directories a file each.
find_files serves sub-roots (src/) from an index rooted above them.

.hypothesis/ added to DEFAULT_EXCLUDES and ddg_build._SKIP_DIRS: 5,677 of
8,188 indexed files on this checkout (index now 2,361), each extensionless,
so the bash analyzer opened every one.

